+# Investigation: window "Not responding" during shader storage init
+
+Symptom: after a shader-changing update (internal resolution 1x -> 2x, saved pipeline cache no longer matches), the window goes "Not responding" at the title screen for minutes. Goal: keep the window responsive and show "Compiling shaders N / M".
+
+## 1. Which thread pumps messages, and where storage init runs
+
+- The message loop is `SDLWindowedAppContext::RunMainMessageLoop` (`src/ui/windowed_app_context_sdl.cpp:87-97`). It calls `SDL_WaitEvent` and `ProcessEvent` on the UI thread. `windowed_app_main_sdl.cpp:75` starts it for the app.
+- Wakeup events run `WindowedAppContext::ExecutePendingFunctionsFromUIThread` (`src/ui/windowed_app_context_sdl.cpp:100-102`, body at `src/ui/windowed_app_context.cpp:138-159`). The queue lock is released while each function runs, so the functions execute on the UI thread.
+- `ReXApp::LaunchModule` queues its work with `app_context().CallInUIThreadDeferred(...)` (`src/ui/rex_app.cpp:465`). The lambda therefore runs on the UI thread from the pending-function drain.
+- `GraphicsSystem::InitializeShaderStorage(..., true)` is called directly inside that lambda at `src/ui/rex_app.cpp:498`. **Yes, it runs on the UI thread.** `main_thread->Resume()` (`rex_app.cpp:503`) only happens after it returns.
+- Inside `GraphicsSystem::InitializeShaderStorage` (`src/graphics/graphics_system.cpp:342-368`):
+  - Blocking path, command processor not paused (`:355-362`): it posts the work with `CallInThread` and then calls `fence.Wait()` at `:361`. **The UI thread blocks on this fence** for the whole translation and pipeline creation. Nothing pumps SDL events or paints ImGui in that time, which is what Windows sees as "Not responding".
+  - Blocking path, paused (`:351-354`): runs inline on the calling (UI) thread, so it blocks the same way.
+  - Non-blocking path (`:363-367`): posts to the command processor thread and returns immediately. The UI thread is not blocked.
+- The `blocking` flag is passed straight to the backends: `D3D12CommandProcessor::InitializeShaderStorage` (`src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp:156-159`) and `PipelineCache::InitializeShaderStorage` (`src/graphics/d3d12/pipeline_cache.cpp:237`). The base `CommandProcessor` version is a no-op (`src/graphics/command_processor.cpp:403-404`).
+
+## 2. What `PipelineCache::InitializeShaderStorage` does on a mismatch
+
+What is checked (`src/graphics/d3d12/pipeline_cache.cpp:259-337`):
+- The `.xpso` header (`:285-296`) holds only magic, API and version (`PipelineDescription::kVersion`, `Modification::kVersion`). It does not encode the resolution scale or any game-shader identity.
+- Each stored description is checked with XXH3 against its own stored `description_hash` (`:317-322`). The `.xsh` ucode is checked the same way against its own `ucode_data_hash` (`:476-480`). Both are file-integrity checks. On failure the stream is truncated (`:320`, `:478`).
+- Nothing in this path compares stored entries with the shaders the running game produces. Pipelines whose shaders are missing or fail translation are skipped silently (`:589-591`, `:597`, `:603-605`, `:611`, `:632-633`), not rebuilt.
+- **Not verified:** why 1x -> 2x makes the saved cache stop matching. The translator is built with `draw_resolution_scale_x/y` (`:393-394`), but this pass did not find where a mismatch would be detected. Treat the cause as open.
+
+Shader phase (`:345-545`):
+- Shader translation runs on **a pool of helper threads**: `shader_translation_thread_function` (`:387-463`). The pool size is `min(busy + queued + 1, logical_processor_count - 1)` (`:494-506`). Each thread does `AnalyzeUcode` and `TranslateAnalyzedShader` (`:423-447`).
+- The main stored-shader loop (`:466-515`) reads ucode from the file and queues shaders for translation. `shaders_translated` (`:514`) counts queued shaders, not finished ones. It then waits for the pool (`:516-525`).
+- Translation is **synchronous with respect to the caller**: the call does not return until every helper thread has joined.
+
+Pipeline phase (`:547-716`):
+- Each stored description is resolved and turned into a `Pipeline` (`:567-673`). Pipelines are queued for creation on the creation pool (`:661-667`). The pool is created once, in the constructor (`:168-181`), from `d3d12_pipeline_creation_threads` (default -1 = 3/4 of logical processors, `:171`), capped by logical processors. `creation_thread_needed_count` (`:554`) is computed but never used: the loop at `:557` cannot add threads, so the pool does not grow here.
+- The main thread drains the queue through `CreateQueuedPipelinesOnProcessorThread` (call at `:676`, definition at `:3311-3330`). It runs on the calling thread and does not set the completion event.
+- The completion event is set in `CreationThread` (definition `:3264`, `Set()` at `:3273-3276`) by a pool thread that finds the queue empty with no busy threads.
+- When `blocking` is true, the call waits on `creation_completion_event_` (`:697-706`). Nothing waits in the non-blocking case.
+- The storage writer thread is created at the end (`:739`).
+
+Progress counter: **none exists**. The only counts are locals: `shaders_translated` (`:377`, `:514`, logged at `:535`) and `pipelines_created` (`:566`, `:672`, logged at `:710-715`). Nothing is published while the work runs. The total M for pipelines is `pipeline_stored_descriptions.size()`, known after the read at `:307-310` (it is an upper bound: entries skipped at `:583-633` are still counted). A shader total is not known until the `.xsh` loop finishes (`:466-515`).
+
+## 3. Existing overlay / notification infrastructure
+
+- ImGui is set up in `ReXApp::SetupOverlays` (`src/ui/rex_app.cpp:422-424`), with `OnCreateDialogs` at `:461`. Dialogs are `ImGuiDialog` subclasses; `ImGuiDialog::Draw` is at `src/ui/imgui_dialog.cpp:44`. Draws run from the paint path (`src/ui/window_sdl.cpp:532-534` → `Window::OnPaint`, `src/ui/window.cpp:675`), i.e. on the UI thread.
+- Existing overlays: console, settings, achievements, debug (`src/ui/overlay/*.cpp`). Achievement toasts (`src/ui/overlay/achievement_toast.cpp:32`) are the closest model for a non-modal notification.
+- `ReXApp::LaunchModule` already registers a notification dialog (`rex_app.cpp:469-482`).
+- No existing progress/loading dialog. A new `ImGuiDialog` subclass would be needed (it can be modeled on `AchievementToastDialog`).
+
+## 4. Smallest responsive change
+
+Recommended approach (keeps the existing fence pattern, moves the blocking call off the UI thread):
+
+1. `src/ui/rex_app.cpp:493-513` (in `LaunchModule`): run `graphics_system->InitializeShaderStorage(cache_root, title_id, true)` on a worker thread (e.g. `rex::thread::Thread::Create`, or `std::thread`, as `module_thread_` already does at `:505`). The UI thread returns from the lambda immediately.
+2. Move `OnPostLaunchModule(main_thread.get())` and `main_thread->Resume()` (`:502-503`) and the `module_thread_` creation (`:505-512`) into a completion step that the worker posts back with `app_context().CallInUIThread(...)`. This keeps the guest from starting before storage is ready.
+3. Show progress: a new `ImGuiDialog` subclass that reads atomic counters and draws "Compiling shaders N / M". Show it from `OnCreateDialogs` or from `LaunchModule`, and remove it in the completion step.
+4. Progress counters: add `std::atomic<size_t>` members to `PipelineCache` at the **end** of the class in `include/rex/graphics/d3d12/pipeline_cache.h` (after `creation_threads_busy_` at `:422`, before the closing `};` at `:435`). Update them at `pipeline_cache.cpp:514` (shaders) and `:672` (pipelines). Set the total M from `pipeline_stored_descriptions.size()` after the read at `:307-310`. Initialize the counters to 0 in their declarations. Expose them through a new const getter on `D3D12CommandProcessor`/`GraphicsSystem` (added at the end of each class only).
+5. Do not change any existing member order in `GraphicsSystem`, `PipelineCache`, or `CommandProcessor`. Only append.
+
+Alternative (smaller, but riskier): pass `blocking=false` from `rex_app.cpp:498` (`graphics_system.cpp:363-367`). The UI thread is free right away, but the guest may start before pipelines exist. Draws with missing pipelines are not verified here, so this would need checking in the D3D12 draw path before relying on it.
+
+## Risks
+
+- **Thread affinity**: the translation and pipeline creation already run on the command processor thread today. `GraphicsSystem::InitializeShaderStorage` posts the work with `CallInThread` (`graphics_system.cpp:357-358`, `command_processor.cpp:406-412`) and the UI thread waits on the fence (`:361`). The D3D12 objects stay on that same thread. Moving the call to a worker only changes **who waits on the fence**: the worker blocks and the UI thread keeps pumping. The pool threads (`pipeline_cache.cpp:559-560`) already make D3D12 calls off the command processor thread, as they do today.
+- **Real concurrency risk**: `CommandProcessor::pending_fns_` is a `std::queue` with no lock (`include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h:244`), and `CallInThread` pushes to it without one (`command_processor.cpp:406-412`). Verified this pass. Any other producer calling `CallInThread` at the same time as the worker (e.g. `graphics_system.cpp:335`, `:339`, `:344`, or the presenter) is a data race. Either keep all init-time producers on one thread, or add a mutex to `CommandProcessor` (appended at the end of the class) and lock it in `CallInThread` and in the drain loop.
+- **Paused path**: if the command processor is paused, `graphics_system.cpp:351-354` runs the work on the calling thread. On a worker that is fine per the existing comment, but it means the worker does the work, not the UI thread. Verify the launch path is not paused.
+- **What waits on storage**: `main_thread->Resume()` (`rex_app.cpp:503`) and the guest thread start. Any other code that assumes pipelines exist after `LaunchModule` must be gated too. Not checked in this pass.
+- **Shutdown during init**: if the window closes while the worker runs, `shutting_down_` (`rex_app.cpp:509`) and the module-thread lambda must be checked. Joining the worker in the destructor is needed.
+- **Exported classes**: the game exe is built against the unpatched headers. The changes above only append members, so no layout change is introduced for existing members. A new dialog class and new getters must not change any existing vtable order (virtual methods only appended, if at all).
+- **Not verified here**: no build or tests were run (read-only investigation). `CreateQueuedPipelinesOnProcessorThread` (`pipeline_cache.cpp:3311-3330`) was read, but the rest of the draw path was not checked for missing-pipeline behavior. The 1x -> 2x cause is still open (section 2).
